intments (MAs/referrals/home reports/viewings).</p><p>- Ensure readiness for Platform update on **2026-04-20** and training on **2026-05-06**.</p><p>### Agreed Actions</p><p>| Action | Owner | Deadline |</p><p>| --- | --- | --- |</p><p>| Investigate and resolve reporting inconsistency (apps vs purchase/remortgage split; NTUs) | Bob | Not stated |</p><p>| Produce quarterly written vs banked forecast | Bob Duncan | 2026-04-23 |</p><p>| Produce purchase seasonality forecast | Bob Duncan | 2026-04-23 |</p><p>| Confirm and own 2026 target of **72 purchase cases/year** (≈ **1.5/week**) and maintain pace | Roland | Ongoing (from 2026-04-08) |</p><p>| Validate lead flow assumption (**~480/year**) and feasibility of **30–35 conversations/month** | Bob + Roland | Not stated |</p><p>| Practice Platform navigation in demo case **John Smith** | Roland + Megan | 2026-04-10 |</p><p>| Calculate and share quarterly targets for written/banked + cases | Bob Duncan | 2026-04-10 (or w/c 2026-04-13 if delayed) |</p><p>| Adopt Platform task workflow for follow-ups (post update) | Roland + Admin | From 2026-04-20 |</p><p>| Confirm admin cover plan (Megan maternity leave risk) | Ops/Management | 2026-05-06 |</p><p>| If circumstances change during the week, CRM must be updated immediately and blockers flagged early. |  |  |</p><p>| Bob |  |  |</p><p>Full transcript</p><p>Speaker 1: Excuse me. Too bad.</p><p>Roland Brownlee: Good, you getting okay?</p><p>Megan Gordon: I was getting an X-ray done. I&#x27;ve got a slipped rib. It&#x27;s very uncomfortable.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Oh gosh, she&#x27;s making that up. How can you have a slipped rib?</p><p>Megan Gordon: How can you have a slipped rib?</p><p>Bob Duncan: You&#x27;re not gonna ask, probably, for this call.</p><p>Megan Gordon: I&#x27;ve got hypermobility, so my bones are already loose and can pop out of place. And because of all the new hormones that also make your bones loose, the rib has moved from where it&#x27;s meant to be.</p><p>Roland